PREAMBLE

Apoli and Origins are distributed under a fairly open license. Read it if you
want to do anything with them besides play.

You are free to use, share and adapt both mods. Nobody can take those rights
away from you as long as you follow the terms below.

If you only want to play, or you are writing a data pack or an addon, none of
this is likely to affect you. Read section 4, "Building on Apoli", and carry
on.


1. GENERAL CLAUSES

   These apply on top of every other section of this license.

   1.1 Extent
       This license covers Apoli, Origins, the Handbook website, and all
       other code, assets and binaries in their repositories, unless a file
       says otherwise. Where a bundled file carries its own license, that
       license applies to that file.

   1.2 Waiver
       Any restriction in this license can be set aside with personal
       permission. Read clause 1.3 before asking.

   1.3 Personal Permission
       Personal permission is rarely granted, and usually only when there's a
       good reason for it, because granting it reads as an endorsement. If
       what you want to do is already allowed below, you don't need to ask,
       and asking will most likely get you pointed back at this license.

   1.4 Informal
       This license will not hold up in court, and nobody intends to take
       anyone there. The realistic worst case for breaking it is being asked
       to put it right, although a distribution platform such as Modrinth or
       CurseForge may also take your project down. Breaking it also makes you
       a jerk, and you don't want to be a jerk, do you?


2. DISTRIBUTING THE MODS

   This covers making the binaries, assets or source available somewhere
   other than the original download pages: in a modpack, on a mirror, or
   bundled with a server.

   2.1 Modpack (ALLOWED)
       You may put either mod in a modpack without asking, whether the pack
       is public, private or made for one server. That is what the mods are
       for.

   2.2 Attribution
       Credit Overgrown as the author of the parts you are distributing. If
       you changed anything, say so. A link back is optional but appreciated.

   2.3 Non-Monetary (NOT ALLOWED)
       You may not charge for access to the distribution or make money from
       it in any other way. That includes ad-gated links and URL shorteners,
       download services that slow you down unless you pay, and putting any
       part of the download behind a paywall. Selling in-game goods or
       cosmetics on a server is not distribution, so it is between you and
       the Minecraft EULA.


3. FEATURING THE MODS

   This covers using either mod somewhere you are not handing out binaries,
   assets or source, such as a video, a stream, a review or a public server.

   3.1 Free Rein (ALLOWED)
       Go ahead. You don't need permission or to ask first, and you may
       monetise the video or stream as usual. The Non-Monetary Clause (2.3)
       is about distributing the files, not about your content.

   3.2 Thief (NOT ALLOWED)
       Do not claim you made either mod. Crediting Overgrown makes you
       cooler, but it is not required.


4. BUILDING ON APOLI

   This covers writing a data pack, or a Java addon that registers its own
   power, action and condition types against the Apoli API.

   4.1 Data Pack (ALLOWED)
       Data packs and resource packs you write are entirely yours. Powers,
       origins, layers and badges are your content, not a derivative of the
       mod, and nothing in this license applies to them. License and sell
       them however you like.

   4.2 Addon (ALLOWED)
       An addon that depends on Apoli and calls its API is not a derivative
       work of it. Your addon is yours, under any license you choose
       (including a closed one), as long as you do not copy Apoli's own code
       into it. Addons are what the engine is for, and the Addon docs
       (https://0vergrown.github.io/Handbook/docs/addon) exist to help you
       write one.

   4.3 Compatibility (ALLOWED)
       You may ship compatibility code for Apoli or Origins in your own mod,
       including mixins into them, without asking. Please use the public API
       where one exists so your compatibility code doesn't break with every
       update.


5. USING THE CODE OR ASSETS

   This covers copying source, textures or models out of either mod into
   your own project, or forking one of them. It is the only section with
   real conditions attached.

   5.1 Attribution
       Credit Overgrown as the author of the parts you are using, and say so
       if you altered them.

   5.2 Copyleft
       Your project must be open source, with its source visible and
       redistribution and modification allowed, and it must carry a clause
       much like this one.

   5.3 Fork (ALLOWED)
       You may fork either mod, including to keep an old version alive or to
       take it somewhere this one is not going. Give your fork a distinct
       name and mod ID so nobody installs it expecting this one.

   5.4 Upstream
       Both mods are reimplementations of apace100's original Apoli and
       Origins and inherit obligations from them. Where a file traces back to
       that work, its original license travels with it, and this license
       cannot remove those terms.


NO WARRANTY

The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied. The author is not liable for any claim, damages or other liability
arising from the software or its use.


